<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
<Document>
<name>SINS OF OUR FATHERS mission map — detailed rev2 updated</name>
<description>Normalized geometry-and-notes transcription of the latest owner KML. 152 placemarks: 145 points, 6 LineStrings, 1 Polygon. Owner updates and continuity corrections folded in 2026-08-08. Planning/reference geometry only; production island is subject to the locked east-west fictionalization mirror.</description>
<Placemark>
<name>Crimson Two&apos;s position</name>
<description>Lawrence "Rip" Mansell occupies a mobile observation tower inside the fortified bermed area that also contains the I-Dome autonomous air-defense battery, at the island&apos;s highest point of elevation. EXTREME PREJUDICE is equipped with a high-powered thermal optic, making foliage and other partial visual concealment less reliable; the player needs true line-of-sight breaks, hard cover, or a sufficiently advantageous firing solution. After defeating Mansell, the player can recover EXTREME PREJUDICE from his observation post.</description>
<Point>
<coordinates>-64.82642382189304,18.29974081145582,0</coordinates>
</Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>Covert floatplane landing location</name>
<description>This is where smoke coast the plane to a landing with an engine off allowing Victor Two Bravo to access the island undetected via an unlit disused boat launch..</description>
<Point>
<coordinates>-64.8228,18.2977615,0</coordinates>
</Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>Concealed staging area</name>
<description>The team make their way here to allow Tripper to asses physical and network security measures that the team should be aware of, and to allow time for the team to review, finalize, and agree on the mission objective approach plan.</description>
<Point>
<coordinates>-64.8233874,18.298763,0</coordinates>
</Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>Temple Pavilion</name>
<description>This eclectically and expensively decorated pavilion styled to look like an Egyptian temple contains a secure office used by Goldberg. Inside, the player can find Intel collectibles, and the other CheyTac M200 Intervention sniper rifle. The rifle can be used to defeat Rip from a distance.</description>
<Point>
<coordinates>-64.8281808,18.298149,0</coordinates>
</Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>Western cape pool house flagpole base stash location.</name>
<description>This is where the player may find Regent&apos;s Intel dead drop, hidden behind a loose stone block in the flag pole base near the pool house. Cache details: weatherproof cache or sealed container;one encrypted USB drive;handwritten note;unfamiliar symbol;coordinates that do not correspond to a Game 1 objective;no signature. the player can reveal the location of this stash by collecting and piecing together the coordinate fragments scattered across 8 benches on the island</description>
<Point>
<coordinates>-64.8285678,18.3012709,0</coordinates>
</Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>Crimson Three&apos;s position</name>
<description>The player approaches along the eastern beach using foliage for cover from drones. The main access route is too heavily surveilled and protected by automated weapons systems for the team to risk. The team therefore works around to the northwestern guesthouse/service side of the main-residence property and uses the guesthouse service entrance. The guesthouse contains a concealed security-monitoring room. After defeating Dermot "Lucky" Underwood, the player can recover his access card and alter local IFF threat profiles so Goldberg’s automated defenses can be turned against Crimson One. The exact IFF-assisted result remains implementation-open: it may suppress, injure, displace, or defeat Graves, while direct combat remains valid. Shortly after the team enters the dark, apparently deserted guesthouse, Underwood attacks with a stun grenade, initiating a frantic close-quarters firefight.</description>
<Point>
<coordinates>-64.8246302551776,18.30344069786174,0</coordinates>
</Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>Crimson One&apos;s position</name>
<description>The mezzanine on the first floor level of the main residence&apos;s entry hall is where the player finds Graves expecting him, already in cover. Unless the player tampers with the IFF settings beforehand, trying to defeat Graves in a full-on fight is tricky and rewarding challenge. The player can also find many Intel collectibles by searching the large residence before proceeding to the helipad for the final part of the mission.</description>
<Point>
<coordinates>-64.82429260000001,18.302896,0</coordinates>
</Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>Final helipad confrontation location</name>
<description>The player moves through the main residence&apos;s courtyard and across the driveway to the helipad, where the team confronts Goldberg and Stockbridge as they prepare to escape. CIA Director Macmillan intervenes by radio and orders the team to stand down and allow Goldberg and Stockbridge to leave by helicopter. Spook refuses, prompting Bishop to declare Victor Two Bravo rogue and ending the campaign finale on a cliffhanger while the targets escape.</description>
<Point>
<coordinates>-64.8235337,18.3025516,0</coordinates>
</Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>Boath launch access point</name>
<Point>
<coordinates>-64.82269059999999,18.2978334,15.53961950354232</coordinates>
</Point>
</Placemark>
