<Placemark>
<name>northwestern beach bungalow</name>
<description>Contains collectible Intel in the form of a flash drive and a file containing several printouts of highly compromising and incriminating photos showing then president-elect Barry James Crodyn and SCOTUS justices Walter Pedilla and Creighton Howard engaging in multiple acts of immoral and illicit conduct.</description>
<Point>
<coordinates>-64.82474159650387,18.30253543560128,11.88302519737619</coordinates>
</Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>boat</name>
<description>This boat is noninteractable, and found partially loaded with boxed supplies, that seem to have been prepared for an evacuation. It suggests that someone attempted to use it to escape the island after the invasion, but it never actually left. A set of discarded ligatures, a half empty backpack, and a few old blood smears can also be found. There is no body. The port is otherwise deserted.</description>
<Point>
<coordinates>-64.82534773829053,18.30225061423911,0.4526213764534543</coordinates>
</Point>
</Placemark>
