<Placemark>
<name>I-Dome mobile air defense system battery location</name>
<description>Goldberg&apos;s I-Dome autonomous air-defense battery occupies the fortified bermed site at the island&apos;s high point. The battery is unlit and has its own panoramic light-amplifying security camera on a shorter pole near the radar mast. Tampering or significant disturbance is reported to security control, which can dispatch a reconnaissance UAV from the main-residence rooftop dock; confirmed intrusion can escalate to armed enforcer UAVs. Repeated or reckless aggressive engagement of those enforcer UAVs can drive the local security state high enough to activate heavier autonomous ground systems, including ThreeHalf heavy Q-UGVs. The property-security architecture remains Goldberg-controlled, local, and isolated from PANDORA and wider strategic networks.</description>
<Point>
<coordinates>-64.82660821953912,18.29959903430874,49.0027131009921</coordinates>
</Point>
</Placemark>
