<Placemark>
<name>vantage point</name>
<description>The extra height and decent foliage cover make this place exceptionally well-suited for a long-range kill shot. But getting the M200 from the Temple Pavilion, and then making this considerable detour. Players attempting to take the shot with GRAY GHOST should find it to be considerably challenging, but not completely impossible to get a one-shot kill, especially with subsonics, given that they lack the effective range for even a skilled shooter to confidently land a well-placed first shot. If the player opts to fire supersonic ammo, Crimson Two is promptly able to locate the player and return fire (using a suppressor slightly extends the time I takes Rip to locate the player, but it is not a magically prevent him from being able to identify the player&apos;s position). The M200 makes pulling a one shot kill from this position a much more manageable, but nonetheless rewarding task.</description>
<Point>
<coordinates>-64.82238708007374,18.29731431124392,21.40201353156567</coordinates>
</Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>ThreeHalf Q-UGV dock</name>
<description>ThreeHalves are centaur-like heavy quadrupedal autonomous UGVs. They are extremely difficult to disable once active, but the player can avoid fighting them entirely. They normally remain docked and in standby. A sufficiently high local alarm state—especially one caused by recklessly and repeatedly engaging enforcer UAVs—or a direct attack on a ThreeHalf can activate them into combat mode. If Victor Two Bravo reaches a docking station stealthily while a ThreeHalf is still docked and dormant, Tripper can sabotage the docked unit&apos;s power-management circuits, causing it to shut down without waking. The sabotage route is optional and rewards stealth rather than requiring a ThreeHalf fight. Active ThreeHalves carry modified belt-fed AR-15-pattern automatic rifles with spare linked ammunition carried on the rear body.</description>
<Point>
<coordinates>-64.8245222288221,18.30179278935379,8.589646129059449</coordinates>
</Point>
</Placemark>
